    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **258 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization applied when an owner is created, in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (the only place owners are created \u2014 V2 is read-only).\n\n**New helper methods** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- `normaliseAddress(String)` \u2014 trims and collapses internal whitespace, upper-cases, and expands common street abbreviations (`ST \u2192 STREET`, `RD \u2192 ROAD`, `AVE \u2192 AVENUE`). A `null` input maps to the empty string. Abbreviation expansion is token-based and tolerates a trailing period, so both `St` and `St.` expand to `STREET`.\n- `expandAddressAbbreviation(String)` \u2014 the per-token expansion used above.\n\n**Changes to `addOwner`**:\n1. The raw address is normalized up front via `normaliseAddress`.\n2. **Required-field check**: if the address is blank *after* normalization, the request is rejected with `400 BAD_REQUEST`. (The OpenAPI DTO pattern `(?s).*\\S.*` already blocks whitespace-only input at bean-validation time, so this controller check is the belt-and-suspenders guarantee the spec calls for.)\n3. **Household duplicate detection** now compares the normalized form of both the incoming address and each existing owner's address (`normaliseAddress(existing.getAddress())`), instead of the old lower-casing `normaliseIdentity`.\n4. **Shared household id** is seeded from the normalized address (`addressKey = address`), so household grouping is consistent with the stored value.\n5. The **stored/returned address** is set to the normalized value via `owner.setAddress(address)`.\n\nOwner update (`updateOwner`) was intentionally left unchanged, since the spec scopes normalization to owner *creation*.\n\nBehaviorally, an owner created with `\"  110   W. Liberty St.  \"` is now stored and returned as `\"110 W. LIBERTY STREET\"`, and duplicate/household logic keys off that canonical form.",
